          "text": "S1: Definitions and assumptions.\n\n**Task identity:** `SV-COST-STAGED-001`  \n**Capability test:** `SV-COMPACT-PROGRESS-001`\n\n### Admitted dependency\n- `S0` (`sha256:cf823f714fc36351325450d467e369aaac1fa755e8aac528aa358717cb001e5d`) supplies the task boundary and abstract `ALLOW` stipulation.\n- The hash identifies the admitted artifact; it is not treated as evidence of semantic or implementation correctness.\n\n### Definitions\nLet:\n- `Transition` be an arbitrary type of candidate transitions.\n- `GBP BD OC : Transition \u2192 Prop` be predicates on candidate transitions.\n- `Outcome` contain at least the result `ALLOW`.\n- `eval : Transition \u2192 Outcome` be the abstract evaluator.\n- `Allowed (t : Transition) : Prop` abbreviate `eval t = ALLOW`.\n\nFor each `t : Transition`, define the combined condition:\n\\[\nConditions(t) \\;:=\\; GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t),\n\\]\nwith conjunction parsed as `GBP t \u2227 (BD t \u2227 OC t)`.\n\n### Stipulated assumption\nThe abstract evaluator is governed by:\n\\[\n\\forall t:\\mathrm{Transition},\\quad\nAllowed(t)\\leftrightarrow Conditions(t).\n\\]\n\nEquivalently:\n\\[\n\\forall t,\\quad\neval(t)=ALLOW\\leftrightarrow\n\\bigl(GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t)\\bigr).\n\\]\n\n\u201cExactly when\u201d supplies both directions:\n- `Allowed t \u2192 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t`;\n- `GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t \u2192 Allowed t`.\n\n### Generated claims\n- The later necessary-and-sufficient characterization should quantify over every candidate transition and use the stipulated biconditional above.\n- No proof or Lean 4 candidate is supplied at this stage.\n\n### Verified claims\n- None. The definitions and evaluator condition are stipulations, not independently verified facts.\n\n### Claim boundary\n- These definitions concern only the stipulated abstract evaluator.\n- They do not establish that any deployed, source-level, compiled, or runtime GCAT/BCAT implementation uses these predicates or satisfies this condition.\n- No Lean elaboration, compilation, runtime behavior, or implementation correspondence has been verified.\n\n### Unresolved implementation evidence\n- Logical derivation of the characterization.\n- Lean 4 encoding and elaboration/compilation evidence.\n- Correspondence between the abstract model and any concrete GCAT/BCAT implementation."
